id: pm-tzutu5
title: "Intent reads that tip over budget only with receipts settle in universal row compaction, which yields fewer rows per page than the overhead-charged intent pass on session-bounded reads"
description: "Found in the Codex review of PR #1758 (the pm-gh1753 fix). An intent read can tip over its budget only once the read-output receipts join the envelope. pm-gh1753's estimate mirror now settles such a page in the universal read-output compaction. That compaction drops rows and adds continuation metadata (output_budget_truncation, an output cursor), which itself costs room. Before the fix, the same page went through the intent layer's overhead-charged second pass, reached by the receipt-digit drift. That pass shrank the intent page and only rebased the cheaper producer next_cursor. Codex's repro: a TOON triage read with outputBudget 1000 and 1,309 tokens left in its output session. The six-row intent page measures 1,001 with receipts. The release that pm-gh1753 fixed returned five rows at 910 tokens; the fix returns three rows plus an output cursor, and with the session's remaining budget, following that cursor yields a budget omission. No row is lost: every row stays reachable through the cursor, in a new session if needed. But the first page yields fewer rows, and the session reaches fewer rows. Choosing the cheaper strategy deliberately, rather than by accident, is the work: try the overhead-charged intent projection before accepting a universally compacted intent page, and keep whichever delivers more rows within both ceilings. Cursors must stay bound to the first pass's uncompacted prefix (pm-gh1753's binding)."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 3
tags[6]: "area:output",intent,output-budget,read-output,row-yield,session
created_at: "2026-11-19T11:24:11.391Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-19T11:42:38.754Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "For an intent read whose settled envelope exceeds the intent budget only through read-output receipts, the delivered page is the candidate with more rows among the overhead-charged intent projection and the universally compacted page, both within the intent and session ceilings; Output cursors of either candidate replay against unchanged rows (the pm-gh1753 binding), and the 1,476-configuration replay harness stays at zero stale cursors; A spec reproduces the session-bounded triage case (outputBudget 1000, 1,309 session tokens left) and delivers at least the prior five rows"
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: medium
confidence: medium
severity: low
expected_result: "An intent page that exceeds its budget only once receipts are included is delivered by whichever compaction (overhead-charged intent pass or universal row compaction) keeps more rows within both the intent and session ceilings, with output cursors bound to the first pass's uncompacted prefix."
actual_result: "The universal compaction always settles it: Codex's session-bounded triage repro delivers three rows plus an output cursor where the prior release delivered five rows at 910 tokens."
