notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-19T11:42:38.753Z","harness:claude-code","Narrowed by PR #1758: the refusal variant is fixed there. A page the read-output stage would refuse outright is now decided again with the receipts' overhead charged to the intent pass (chargedIntentPassOrRefusal, recorded on pm-gh1753). What remains here is the yield preference: when universal compaction does deliver rows, but fewer than the overhead-charged intent pass would, still choose the pass that keeps more rows."
